Z||000000||Philphine||09-10-2001||11:14 AM||||<BR>i saw in another thread where the pontiac lights in the tail are somehow connected to the cooling system. neither of mine work (the fan dose if i turn on the air. didn't occur to me to see if the lights maybe came on too).<P>if this is so i'm wondering if there may be other interconnected problems that i'm not linking together. i'm not much of a mechanic and my fiero experience is all with 4clys. i've also lost my hanes manual and i'm trying not to use murphy's law to find it yet (the best way to find something lost is to go get one just like it) some i know can't be connected but i'll take any help i can get.<P>fan comes on only with a/c on<P>no pontiac lights in tail (don't care at the moment beyond it's being connected to another prob as stated)<P>temp real unstable. will go into red on gauge and i'll turn it off a sec. turn it back on and it comes down. so far all i've done is change to a 180 deg. thermostat and play with the fan manually (turn ac off and on). it still dose it on start but will eventually move almost off scale cold or sometimes go to midscale and drop to cold again. burp? sending unit? haven't tried yet.<P>high idle. can't get it below 13-1500rpm. this is where i started working first. changed iac then started looking for a vaccume leak. if i spray carb cleaner around/under the throttle body i get a reaction, but it takes a big long spray to get it to react, so i guess it's a small leak and i haven't found it yet. dosen't the idle circuit get something from the tempeture to let it know it's warmed up? connection there?<P>these things bother me most (not the pontiac lights. what was said in the other thread has me wondering). i drove the car all day sunday and it seems basicly good, but these things plus some brake work (and it needs a decent stereo system   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> ) keep it from really being a driver. thanks for any help.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P