Z||000001||StuGood||09-10-2001||12:54 PM||||The "PONTIAC" light in the rear of GT's is wired to come on when you turn the ignition switch on.  Not when you turn the lights on.  Sorry if you already knew this - but apparently quite a few people don't / didn't.<P>To verify the temperature gage wiring, unplug the sender (aft left corner on aft cylinder head, two-pin connector).  Turn ignition on, then go back to the connector, watch the temp. gage through the window.  Ground one terminal, then the other.  When you ground one terminal, the temp. gage should "peg," when you ground the other, the idiot light should come on.<P>If this is a recently-acquired car, changing the coolant (and burping) is probably a good idea and might solve your problem.  Who knows...?<P>The coolant sensor is tells the ECM when the engine's warmed up.  It's screwed into the far right end of the lower intake manifold, oriented horizontally.  Two-pin connector also.  There's a bunch of wire bundles and stuff over on that side of the engine, so it's not the easiest thing to access.<P>For the vacuum leak/ high idle problem, remember there are two vacuum lines (vinyl tubes - "blackaroni" - with little rubber elbows) that are supposed to be plugged into the bottom of the throttle body.  Maybe one or both came off?  Hope so -  that would be an easy fix!   ||||reg||3
